  "page1": {
    "title": "A Heart Full of Thanks",
    "subtitle": "Noticing the small kindnesses around us and learning to say thank you.",
    "body": "Think about your morning today. Someone made your breakfast warm. Someone washed the shirt you wear.\n\nWe often miss these kind acts. We see them as just normal. But a thankful heart starts when we notice them.\n\nGratitude means feeling glad for what others give us. It grows stronger when we say it out loud. So we tell our parents, \"Thank you for dinner.\"\n\nWe <mark>show our thanks</mark> with small words and acts. A short note can make a friend smile. Helping with dishes is a way to say thanks too.\n\nWhen we share thanks, our own heart feels warm. The people around us feel happy because of it. A small \"thank you\" can change a whole day. So let us notice the good and share it.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/venus/2026-07/14.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "A child noticing a warm breakfast and a clean shirt, then writing a small thank-you note."
  },
